 Here is a little Venn diagram to illustrate the solution:

Now, we know that there are $3$ students that take both languages; so, we subtract that $3$ from both numbers:
\begin{align*}
   \text{French} &= 8 - 3 &&= 1 \ , \\
   \text{Spanish} &= 12 - 3 &&= 9
\end{align*}
In addition, we know that there are $3$ students that take both languages; add that $3$ to neither:
\begin{align*}
   \text{French|Spanish} &= 3 &&= 0 \ ,\\
      \text{Neither} &= x &&= 12 \ \\
                          x &= 12 \ .
\end{align*}
Thus, $12$ students take neither language.

